{
  "summary": "Reported: ryan.brooks@brightline.example (Ryan Brooks, former Sales Account Executive, user_id 10) says he is returning as a contractor starting Monday. He wants his account re-enabled and his password reset. Checked: the account status is DISABLED (intentional, from offboarding). Per KB-005, Tier 1 did not reset or unlock it. No reactivation is possible without HR/manager confirmation of the contractor engagement and identity verification by callback. Security concern: the sign-in logs show 2 failed-password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05-03:07 ET, outside his usual hours) from Amsterdam, NL, IP 192.0.2.140, on a HOSTING network, with no MFA. Also, the account record still shows vpn_access=true and sign_in_blocked=false even though the account is disabled. Please have security review the attempts and whether VPN access should be revoked. Still needed: HR/manager confirmation of the rehire, identity verification of the requester, then reactivation and credential setup if approved.",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate requests to re-enable a disabled account; there are also suspicious sign-in attempts"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Ryan, welcome back! Your old account was turned off when you left, and the help desk can't turn a disabled account back on or reset its password. I've sent your request to our Tier 2 team. Before they can turn it back on, HR and your hiring manager need to confirm your contractor start. Please ask your manager or HR contact to confirm your start date and role with IT. Once it's approved and we've confirmed it's you, a technician will call you to finish setting up your sign-in. We'll never send a password by email or in this ticket.",
  "internal_note": "lookup_user: user_id 10 is DISABLED (former Sales AE). Following KB-005 and KB-002 step 2, I did not attempt reset_password or unlock_account. Sign-in logs show 2 failed-password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC from Amsterdam, NL (hosting network, IP 192.0.2.140, no MFA, 03:05 ET). This may be someone trying stolen credentials. The account still shows vpn_access=true and sign_in_blocked=false despite being disabled; I've flagged this for security review. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1). Reactivation needs HR/manager confirmation of the rehire and callback identity verification.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
